---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy | MeltGrid Canada";
const description =
  "How MeltGrid Canada collects, uses and protects the information submitted through the Request My Free Design & Estimate form, including photos and plans.";

const structuredData = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    name: title,
    description,
    url: "https://meltgridcanada.ca/privacy/",
    isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", name: "MeltGrid Canada", url: "https://meltgridcanada.ca" },
    publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "MeltGrid Canada", url: "https://meltgridcanada.ca" },
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://meltgridcanada.ca/" },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Privacy policy" },
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/privacy/" structuredData={structuredData}>
  <section class="ppage">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Privacy policy" }]} />
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
      <h1 class="h-display">How we handle your information</h1>
      <p>
        This page explains what MeltGrid Canada collects when you use this website, in particular the "Request my
        free design &amp; estimate" form, and what we do with it. Last updated September 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--tight">
    <div class="container prose ppage__body">
      <h2>What this policy covers</h2>
      <p>
        This policy covers meltgridcanada.ca and the information you give us through the design and estimate
        request form, by phone, or by email. It does not cover any other site you may reach by following a link
        from this one.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>When you submit a design and estimate request, we collect what you enter in the form:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Project type (residential or commercial) and the areas you want to keep clear</li>
        <li>Surface type and coverage preference</li>
        <li>Approximate dimensions of the area</li>
        <li>Postal code</li>
        <li>Timeline</li>
        <li>Name, phone number and email address</li>
        <li>Any notes you add</li>
        <li>Any photos or plans you choose to attach</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you call or email us instead, we collect whatever you choose to tell us in that conversation or message.</p>

      <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
      <p>
        The form also records the page you submitted it from and, where present, the source information in the
        link you arrived from (such as <code>utm_source</code>, <code>utm_medium</code>, <code>utm_campaign</code>,
        <code>utm_content</code> and <code>utm_term</code>). This tells us which page or campaign a request came
        from; it is stored in your browser only for the current visit (session storage) and is not used to identify
        you personally beyond that.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use it</h2>
      <p>We use the information you submit to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Review your request and confirm it is a fit for us</li>
        <li>
          Prepare a design and estimate, including sharing relevant project details with the manufacturer or the
          qualified trades involved in your project, where that is required to design or quote the work
        </li>
        <li>Contact you about your request by phone or email</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell your information, and we do not use it for purposes unrelated to your request without asking you first.</p>

      <h2>Service providers who process this information</h2>
      <p>
        We use third-party services to run this website and handle form submissions. Using a service provider means
        your information passes through their systems to reach us; it does not mean we have handed over control of
        it, and we only use providers for the specific job described.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Formspree (formspree.io) receives and delivers design and estimate form submissions, including any
          attached photos or plans, to us by email. Formspree is based in the United States, so form submissions
          are processed on servers there. Formspree's own privacy practices are described at
          <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy">formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Hosting provider. This website is hosted by a third-party web hosting provider, which processes standard
          web traffic (such as IP addresses in server logs) to serve the site to your browser.
        </li>
        <li>
          Analytics. This site uses Google Analytics (GA4) to collect standard website usage data — such as pages
          viewed, approximate location and how visitors arrived at the site — with IP addresses shortened. It is not
          connected to your name, email or phone number. You can see Google's own privacy information at
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies and similar technology</h2>
      <p>
        The design and estimate form uses your browser's session storage, not a tracking cookie, to remember
        campaign-source information (see above) for the current visit only; it clears when you close your browser.
        Google Analytics sets its own cookies on this site, as described in its privacy policy linked above.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep design and estimate requests, including any attached photos or plans, for as long as reasonably
        needed to respond to your request and, if a project goes ahead, for the records a project of that kind
        normally requires. If you would like us to delete information we hold about you, contact us and we will do
        so unless we have a legitimate reason to keep it, such as an ongoing project.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps to protect the information you share with us, including sending form submissions
        over an encrypted (HTTPS) connection. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we
        cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Your privacy rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under Canadian privacy law (including PIPEDA, where it applies), you have the right to ask what personal
        information we hold about you, to ask us to correct it, and to withdraw your consent to future contact at
        any time. To do any of these, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@meltgridcanada.ca">info@meltgridcanada.ca</a>.
        If you are not satisfied with our response, you may contact the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of
        Canada.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>This website and its form are intended for adults arranging a property project, not for children.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this page if what we collect or how we use it changes — for example, if we connect a
        different form provider or add a new analytics tool. The "last updated" date at the top of this page
        reflects the most recent change.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy or your information: <a href="mailto:info@meltgridcanada.ca">info@meltgridcanada.ca</a>
        or <a href="tel:+14377745305">437-774-5305</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
